
=== SQL Database in Microsoft Fabric

ifndef::pro[]

SQL Database in Microsoft Fabric is only supported in the professional version of SymmetricDS.

endif::pro[]

ifdef::pro[]

SQL Database in Microsoft Fabric is supported as a write-only target.  See <<Write-Only Node>> for details on setting up a write-only node in SymmetricDS.
It uses the https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/connect/jdbc/download-microsoft-jdbc-driver-for-sql-server[Microsoft JDBC driver].

==== Setup

Set up the node by using the <<Set Up New Replication,Configure Diagram>> or the <<Add Node,Connect Database>> wizard and selecting SQL Database in
Microsoft Fabric as the type.  Use the full host name of the database for the endpoint and the name of the database, including the generated suffix,
for the database name. The following is an example of the JDBC URL:

----
jdbc:sqlserver://<workspace>.database.fabric.microsoft.com:1433;database={<database_name>-<guid>};encrypt=true;trustServerCertificate=false;authentication=ActiveDirectoryServicePrincipal
----

The SQL Database in Microsoft Fabric accepts only Microsoft Entra ID authentication.  SymmetricDS uses the service principal of an Entra app registration.
The credentials are entered in the User Id and Password fields:

[horizontal]
User Id:: The Application (client) ID of the app registration
Password:: A client secret of the app registration

WARNING: The connection string shown by the Fabric portal uses `Authentication=ActiveDirectoryInteractive`.  This mode needs to open a browser for
sign-in whenever it opens a connection, which is not compatible with SymmetricDS.  Use `Authentication=ActiveDirectoryServicePrincipal` instead.

The `fabric` module contains the Microsoft Authentication Library that is required for Entra ID authentication.  The web console downloads it when
the connection is tested, or you can run `symadmin module install fabric` to install it.

==== Permissions

The app registration needs to be granted access in each of the following steps:

. Create an app registration in Microsoft Entra ID and a client secret for it.  Depending on the tenant settings, service principals might need to be
allowed to use Fabric APIs, which is a tenant setting in the Fabric admin portal.
. Grant the app registration access to the database item in Fabric, using the Share action on the SQL database item (or a workspace role) with at least the Read permission.
. Create a database user for the app registration and add it to the roles that SymmetricDS needs.  Connect to the database as an administrator and run the following
script, replacing `<app registration name>` with the display name of the app registration:

[source, Sql]
----
CREATE USER [<app registration name>] FROM EXTERNAL PROVIDER;
ALTER ROLE db_ddladmin ADD MEMBER [<app registration name>];
ALTER ROLE db_datareader ADD MEMBER [<app registration name>];
ALTER ROLE db_datawriter ADD MEMBER [<app registration name>];
----

==== Bulk Loading

SymmetricDS can bulk load SQL Database in Microsoft Fabric with the bulk copy API of the Microsoft JDBC driver.  When a channel uses the bulk data
loader, which the reload channel does by default, SymmetricDS writes the rows of a batch to a staging file and streams them to the database in groups of
10,000 rows.  The rows are copied in the same transaction as the SymmetricDS batch, so a failed batch doesn't leave part of its rows in the table.

No extra setup is needed.  The bulk copy uses the same connection and service principal as the rest of SymmetricDS, and nothing is uploaded to OneLake.
Values of identity columns are loaded as they are sent, and empty strings stay distinct from null values.

endif::pro[]
